-- title:
--   Dual compatibility of supersingular Hecke map with T_Ω
-- statement:
--   Let $p\ge 5$ be a prime, $K$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, $N\ge 1$, and $F=K(\bar\jmath,\bar\jmath_N)$ the subfield `modularFunctionFieldC K N` of $K((q))$ generated by the $q$-expansions $j(q)$ and $j(q^N)$; assume $F$ is a curve over $K$ (principal divisors of degree $0$, finite residue extensions, $\Omega[F/K]$ free of rank one), that every nonzero Kähler differential has a divisor of its orders, that at each place the differential of a uniformiser spans $\Omega[F/K]$, that $\Omega[F/K]\neq 0$, and that $F$ carries a chosen canonical local residue datum at each place. Assume `WeilKaehlerAgree`: for each $\omega\neq 0$ the repartition functional $\lambda_\omega=\mathrm{weilOfKaehler}\,\omega$, $\alpha\mapsto\sum_v \mathrm{Tr}_{K(v)/K}\,\mathrm{res}_v(\alpha_v\cdot\partial_v\omega)$, is nonzero, lies in $\Omega(\mathrm{canonicalDivisorOf}\,\omega)$, and that divisor is maximal with this property. Let $(N:K)\neq 0$, $m\ge 1$, let $SS$ be a finite set of places whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces p N K`, and let $D'$ be a divisor equal to $\mathrm{weightDivisor}_m-1$ at supersingular places whose width divides $m$ and to $\mathrm{weightDivisor}_m$ at all other places. Let $\Theta$ be a $K$-linear map from $\mathrm{SSCarrier}$ in weight $2m$ (functions on the supersingular indices) to the $K$-dual of $\Omega(D')$ satisfying the residue formula $\Theta(v)(\lambda_\omega)=\sum_{x\in SS}\mathrm{kaehlerResidueTerm}\,\omega\,(\tilde v)\,x$, where $\tilde v=\mathrm{liftFun}\,v$ is the chosen lift with prescribed poles and leading coefficients and $\tilde v$ is taken diagonally as a repartition. Let $\ell\neq p$ be a prime not dividing $N$, with the corresponding degeneracy roof field $R=\mathrm{charLDegeneracyRoof}\,K\,N\,\ell$ also satisfying the curve, residue, spanning and nontriviality hypotheses. Let $T_\Omega$ be an endomorphism of $\Omega(D')$ and $s\in K$, $s\neq 0$, such that: every element of $\Omega(D')$ is $0$ or of the form $\lambda_\omega$ with $\omega\neq 0$; $T_\Omega\lambda_\omega=0$ whenever $T^\Omega\omega:=\mathrm{Tr}_{\beta}\bigl((\ell^{m-1}h^{m})\cdot\alpha^{*}\omega\bigr)$ vanishes, where $\alpha,\beta:F\to R$ are the two degeneracy maps and $h$ is the Hecke multiplier; and $T_\Omega\lambda_\omega=s\,\lambda_{T^\Omega\omega}$, with $\lambda_{T^\Omega\omega}\in\Omega(D')$, whenever $T^\Omega\omega\neq0$. Then for every $v$ in the carrier, $\Theta(\mathrm{ssHeckeFun}\,\ell\,v)=s^{-1}\cdot\Theta(v)\circ T_\Omega$.
--
--   This is the dual compatibility step matching the combinatorial Hecke operator on supersingular data, defined by $\ell^{m-1}$ times the leading coefficient of the trace of $\beta(\tilde v)h^{m}$, with the transpose of a Hecke-type endomorphism of the space of Weil differentials $\Omega(D')$, the transport being normalised by the scalar $s$. It is used in the construction of the Hecke-equivariant comparison between supersingular mod $p$ data and differentials on the modular curve, and is invoked by [`ModularCurve.SSHeckeV2.exists_omegaHecke_dualMap_theta_and_exit`](thm.html#ModularCurve.SSHeckeV2.exists_omegaHecke_dualMap_theta_and_exit).
